  \ [… 8,043 characters omitted]  | All products, including archived     |
| POST   | `/admin/products`           | Create a product                     |
| PATCH  | `/admin/products/:id`       | Update a product                     |
| DELETE | `/admin/products/:id`       | Archive a product                    |
| POST   | `/admin/products/:id/restore` | Restore an archived product        |
| GET    | `/admin/customers`          | Customer list with spend             |
| GET    | `/admin/customers/:id`      | Customer detail                      |
| GET    | `/admin/coupons`            | Coupon list                          |
| POST   | `/admin/coupons`            | Create a coupon                      |
| PATCH  | `/admin/coupons/:code`      | Update a coupon                      |
| DELETE | `/admin/coupons/:code`      | Delete a coupon                      |
| GET    | `/admin/reviews`            | All reviews                          |
| DELETE | `/admin/reviews/:id`        | Delete a review                      |

Product filters: `q`, `category`, `stock=out|low`, `sort=featured|newest|price-asc|price-desc|rating|popular`.
Order filters: `status`, `payment`, `q`, `from`, `to`, `page`, `limit`.

### Coupons

Seeded codes:

| Code        | Discount        | Minimum | Active |
| ----------- | --------------- | ------- | ------ |
| `BLOOM10`   | 10% off         | —       | yes    |
| `FRESH15`   | 15% off         | $60     | yes    |
| `WELCOME20` | $20 off         | $50     | yes    |
| `MOTHERFIVE`| 20% off         | $80     | no     |

Coupon amounts are expressed in dollars at the API boundary (a fixed coupon of `20` means
$20). Responses include both `value`/`minSubtotal` in dollars and `valueCents`/`minSubtotalCents`.

## Seed data

`npm run seed` creates 25 products across 6 categories (bouquets, roses, tulips, orchids,
plants, gifts), 9 users (1 admin + 8 customers), 26 historical orders spread over the past
few months, product reviews and the coupons above. Product images are hosted on Unsplash;
each one falls back to a branded gradient if the image cannot be loaded.

## Production

```bash
npm run build          # bundles the storefront into web/dist
JWT_SECRET=<strong> npm start
```

The API serves `web/dist` as static files with an SPA fallback, so a single process serves
the whole site on `PORT`.
