{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p6-43dfecc2","text":"The design is quite good already but feels "generic premium ecommerce" with leaf accents. To make it look like a flower/plant shop, I'd:

1. Introduce a warmer, more botanical palette — deeper botanical greens, dusty rose, terracotta/clay accents, cream paper background.
2. Add texture/pattern: subtle grain, botanical SVG decorations (fern fronds, leaf sprigs), scalloped edges on sections, hand-drawn arch frames around images.
3. Typography: display serif in italic accents, maybe add a handwriting/accent script font for eyebrows ("Caveat" or "Fraunces italic"). Fraunces has italic with SOFT/WONK axes. Use italic Fraunces for accent words.
4. Rounded, organic image shapes (arch / petal masks) instead of plain rectangles.
5. Product cards: arched image tops, petal-shaped hover.
6. Buttons: keep pill, maybe more organic.
7. Add marquee ticker ? Could be too much.

I should scope: an aesthetic refresh touching the shared CSS tokens + key surfaces (Navbar, Hero, Home sections, ProductCard, Footer). Also Shop/ProductDetail pages inherit via product card and CSS.

Let me check remaining storefront pages quickly for hardcoded colors that need coherence: Shop, ProductDetail, Cart, Checkout, Auth, Account, OrderConfirmation. And admin should probably stay functional but inherit tokens.

