{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p7-43dfecc2","text":"The palette is defined centrally. Aesthetic refresh via tokens + targeted component styling will cascade widely.

Plan:
1. Refresh palette in index.css: warmer paper cream, deeper botanical green, terracotta/clay, dusty rose; add fonts (Fraunces italic + a script accent? maybe "Cormorant Garamond"? Keep Fraunces for display but add Fraunces italic). Add texture utilities (paper grain via CSS radial noise? Use an inline SVG data URL feTurbulence as a subtle overlay), botanical ornament utilities, scalloped section edges, arch image masks.
2. Update index.html fonts: add Fraunces italic axis (ital) and maybe "Instrument Serif"? Fraunces supports ital axis: family=Fraunces:ital,opsz,wght@0,9..144,300..700;1,9..144,300..700. Add a handwritten accent font? "Caveat" could look DIY, maybe mismatch. I'd instead use Fraunces italic for accents — more botanical editorial.
3. Navbar: warmer bar, botanical divider, logo with petal mark SVG, softer announcement strip with tiny flowers.
