Returning customers can now pick a saved address in checkout, and the demo customer has two seeded so the flow is visible straight away.

**Checkout**

- [Checkout.jsx](web/src/pages/Checkout.jsx) loads the signed-in customer's addresses and shows a "Saved addresses" panel at the top of the delivery step. Each card carries its label (Home/Studio), recipient and address, with a forest check on the selected one.
- The default address is applied automatically on load, filling name, phone, street, city, county, postal code and country — so a returning customer only reviews the form instead of retyping it.
- Clicking another card swaps the form values. "Use a new address" clears the address fields and deselects the cards, and editing any address field manually deselects too, so a typed address is never mislabelled as a saved one.
- The panel only appears for signed-in users with saved addresses; guests and first-time buyers see the original form unchanged.

**[seed.js](server/src/seed.js)** now gives Wanjiru two saved addresses — Home in Westlands (default) and Studio in Kilimani — both with Kenyan county/postal data, so the picker has something to show after `npm run reset`.

**Verified**

- `npm run build` passes.
- Browser-tested the full flow at 1440 px and 390 px: auto-selected Home populated the form, switching to Studio replaced every field, "Use a new address" emptied them, re-selecting Home restored them, and editing the postal code cleared the selection.
- Placed a real order from the picker: HG-MVPD2Q0T-5I41 saved as `28 Riverside Drive, Westlands | Nairobi | Nairobi County | 00100 | KE` with the saved phone, total KSh 7,128 via M-Pesa.
- Caught and fixed a mobile horizontal overflow caused by the address cards' no-wrap text; the checkout now measures 390 px wide with no overflow at 390 px viewport.
